---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Content Transparency"
  description="How Lythaus combines creator declarations, flags, and staff review."
  canonicalPath="/ai-moderation"
>
  <section class="section">
    <h1>Content Transparency and Review</h1>
    <p>
      Lythaus launches with creator declarations, community flags, and staff
      review. Paid automated detection is not active.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Creator declaration</strong> — each post is labelled
        Human-authored, AI-assisted, or AI-generated.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Community flags</strong> — members can report content that may
        violate policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Staff review</strong> — flagged or uncertain content can be
        marked Under review and assessed by an administrator.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Transparency</h2>
    <p>
      If your post is flagged, you will see the reason and can appeal. Our
      moderation console gives moderators full context before any action is
      taken.
    </p>

    <h2>Appeals</h2>
    <p>
      Appeals are enabled for submission and staff review. Community-vote
      adjudication remains disabled until the governance feature is ready.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
